buildabook — installation

Prerequisites
-------------
An Ada 2022 toolchain with the ada-on-alpine packages installed:

    gcc-gnat 15.x   gprbuild   hbnf   (hbnf pulls in mustache-ada transitively)

The canonical way to get these is the ada-toolchain:edge container image
(built by the ada-on-alpine overlay).  See build.sh.

Building from a release tarball
-------------------------------
    ./configure
    make
    make check        # aunit tests

Building from a git checkout
----------------------------
A checkout has configure.ac, not the generated configure script.  Generate it
first (requires autoconf), then build as above:

    autoconf
    ./configure
    make
    make check

configure options
-----------------
    --prefix=DIR        install prefix            (default /usr/local)
    --bindir=DIR        binaries                  (default PREFIX/bin)
    --mandir=DIR        man pages                 (default PREFIX/share/man)
    GPRBUILD=path       gprbuild to use           (detected)
    GNATMAKE=path       gnatmake to use           (detected, probe only)
    TYPST=path          Typst for `buildabook build` (detected, optional)

configure checks for gprbuild, gnatmake, Ada 2022 support, and that the hbnf
and mustache-ada gpr projects are visible to gprbuild.

Installing
----------
    make install      # installs buildabook + man page, default /usr/local
    make uninstall    # removes what make install put in place

Distribution
------------
    make dist         # buildabook-<version>.tar.gz source tarball

Git hooks
---------
The de-claude git hooks live in githooks/ and are enabled per-clone:

    make install-hooks        # or: git config core.hooksPath githooks
